### Muonic X-rays in the Si/YSO stack with a thicker Al target, one job (scripts/muonic_xray_target.sh runs
### many): as macro/muonic_xray_stack.mac, but with a 20 x 20 x tgtCm cm target centred at z = tgtZ cm and only the
### cosmic muons of 0 - tgtEmax GeV. With the 10 cm lead layer nearly every muon that stops in the target is below
### 1 GeV (3-week run, 1 cm target: 1 of the 1434 stack entries with a target X-ray came from above, median 225 MeV),
### so this samples the signal and the backgrounds of the slow muons at a quarter of the cost of all energies; the
### background of the faster muons is that of the 3-week run (its primaries above tgtEmax). The live time in the run
### tree is that of the muons of 0 - tgtEmax GeV. Needs the aliases stkSeed, stkEvents, stkDir, stkFile, tgtCm, tgtZ
### and tgtEmax.

/tof/det/worldSize 420 420 300 cm
/tof/target/size 20 20 {tgtCm} cm
/tof/target/position 0 0 {tgtZ} cm
/update

/OutputFormat 1
/EventFilter 6
/OutputDirectory {stkDir}
/OutputFile {stkFile}
/gun/seed {stkSeed}
/GeneralParticleSource 2
/tof/cosmic/model expacs
/tof/cosmic/species mu+ mu-
/tof/cosmic/angular all 2 mu+ guan mu- guan
/tof/cosmic/planeCenter 0 0 112 cm
/tof/cosmic/halfX 200 cm
/tof/cosmic/halfY 200 cm
/tof/cosmic/thetaMax 75 deg
/tof/cosmic/energyMin 0 GeV
/tof/cosmic/energyMax {tgtEmax} GeV
/run/beamOn {stkEvents}
